{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA, Anti-inflammatory", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (41.67%) to P1-Hp-1971 L=32%, A=K=18%. GRAVY: 1.38; mol wt: 2359.126: Mol formula: C111H196N26O23S3; Mol ex Coeff: 125 (Disulfide bond). A disulfide bond between residues 10 and 18; Activity: Active against S. aureus ATCC 33591 or USA300 (MRSA, MIC 16-64 ug/ml), E.faecalis JH2-2 (MIC 256 ug/ml), L. monocytogenes (), K.pneumoniae (MIC 512 ug/ml or higher), A. baumannii sensitive (MIC 16-32 ug/ml), A.baumannii IMI, MER, OXA-23, OXA-50 (MIC 128-256 ug/ml), E.coli, S.typhimurium, B.cereus (MIC 256 ug/ml), P.aeruginosa PAO1 (MIC >512 ug/ml), P.aeruginosa AMT0060 (CF) (MIC 256 ug/ml), P. aeruginosa C3719 or LES400 (MIC 64 ug/ml). MOA:bacteria:S. aureus: the peptide appeared to work on membranes. At 3xMIC it rapidly killed USA300. There was membrane permeabilization as well. Resistance development:no:bacteria:S. aureus USA300: MRSA USA300 did not develop resistance to the peptide after 20 passages. In vitro Toxicity: HC50 50% hemo.lytic concentration is 409 ug/ml. Lung fibroblast (i.e. IMR-90) cells, IC50 = 96 ug/ml. Lung epithelial (i.e. BEAS-2B), IC50 120 ug/ml and liver (i.e. HepG2) cells: IC50 359 ug/ml. Anti-inflmmatory: the peptide neutralizes LPS and LTA, reducing the inflammation caused by such bacterial components. Animal model:wax moth: The peptides were effective in vivo within a Galleria mellonella model of MRSA USA300 infection.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "35835775", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "NPJ Biofilms Microbiomes. 2022 Jul 14;8(1):58. doi: 10.1038/s41522-022-00320-0. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03481", "source_id": "AP03481", "source_numeric_id": "03481", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03481", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "In silico identification of two peptides with antibacterial activity against multidrug-resistant Staphylococcus aureus.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA, Anti-inflammatory", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (48%) to Maximin H3 L=24%, K=19%, A=G=14%, I=V=10%. GRAVY: 0.986; mol wt: 2120.683; Mol formula: C99H182N26O24; Mol ex Coeff: 0. Activity: Active against S. aureus ATCC 33591 or USA300 (MRSA, MIC 32 ug/ml), E.faecalis JH2-2 (MIC 128 ug/ml), L.monocytogenes (MIC 512 ug/ml), K.pneumoniae (MIC 512 ug/ml or higher), A. baumannii sensitive (MIC 32-64 ug/ml), A.baumannii IMI, MER, OXA-23, OXA-50 (MIC 64-128 ug/ml), E.coli (MIC 512 ug/ml), S.typhimurium, B.cereus (MIC 256 ug/ml), P.aeruginosa PAO1 (MIC >512 ug/ml), P.aeruginosa AMT0060 (CF) (MIC 256 ug/ml), P. aeruginosa C3719 or LES400 (MIC 64 ug/ml). MOA:bacteria: the peptide appeared to work on membranes. There was membrane permeabilization as well. Resistance development:no:bacteria:S. aureus USA300: MRSA USA300 did not develop resistance to the peptide after 20 passages. In vitro Toxicity: HC50 50% hemo.lytic concentration is 458 ug/ml. Lung fibroblast (i.e. IMR-90) cells, IC50 = 294 ug/ml; Lung epithelial (i.e. BEAS-2B) and liver (i.e. HepG2) cells: IC50 >1000 ug/ml. Anti-inflmmatory: the peptide neutralizes LPS and LTA, reducing the inflammation caused by such bacterial components. Animal model:wax moth: The peptides were effective in vivo within a Galleria mellonella model of MRSA USA300 infection.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "35835775", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "NPJ Biofilms Microbiomes. 2022 Jul 14;8(1):58. doi: 10.1038/s41522-022-00320-0. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03482", "source_id": "AP03482", "source_numeric_id": "03482", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03482", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "In silico identification of two peptides with antibacterial activity against multidrug-resistant Staphylococcus aureus.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
